---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  locale="en" 
  customTitle="Privacy Policy — EpoxyResin-Calculator.com"
  customDescription="Privacy policy for EpoxyResin-Calculator.com. Learn how we handle client-side calculations, cookies, and Google Analytics."
  showLanguageSelector={false}
>
  <div class="py-16 bg-white dark:bg-slate-950 transition-colors duration-200">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      
      <div class="mb-10 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pb-6">
        <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-bold text-cyan-700 dark:text-cyan-400 hover:text-cyan-800 dark:hover:text-cyan-300 mb-4 transition-colors">
          ← Back to Calculator
        </a>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-4xl">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-2">
          Effective Date: January 1, 2026 • Last Updated: September 2026
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-6 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
        
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">1. Client-Side Calculation Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            EpoxyResin-Calculator.com (&quot;we&quot;, &quot;us&quot;, or &quot;our&quot;) is engineered as a privacy-first utility micro-tool. We do not require user accounts, logins, passwords, email subscriptions, or billing details to access any part of our calculator suite.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            All dimension values (Length, Width, Diameter, Depth, Margin of Error, and Specific Gravity ratios) entered into the calculator are evaluated strictly in your local browser runtime memory via client-side JavaScript. <strong>We do not capture, log, or transmit your workshop dimensions, proprietary mold measurements, or resin recipes to our servers or any third-party database.</strong>
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">2. Web Analytics (Google Analytics 4)</h2>
          <p>
            To understand how visitors interact with our calculators, diagnose technical issues, and improve our guides and internationalization features, we use <strong>Google Analytics</strong> (Google LLC).
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Google Analytics collects non-personally identifiable aggregate telemetry such as:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            <li>Approximate geographic location (country and city level; IP addresses are anonymized by default in GA4);</li>
            <li>Browser type, device model, operating system, and screen resolution;</li>
            <li>Referral sources (e.g., search engine queries, referring websites);</li>
            <li>Page visits, navigation paths, session duration, and feature interactions (such as unit switches or language selections).</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Google Analytics does not collect personally identifiable information (PII) like names or physical addresses, and it does not link your website visits to personal identity records. For more details on how Google handles data, please consult <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-cyan-700 dark:text-cyan-400 underline hover:text-cyan-800 dark:hover:text-cyan-300">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a> and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-cyan-700 dark:text-cyan-400 underline hover:text-cyan-800 dark:hover:text-cyan-300">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">3. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
          <p>
            Google Analytics utilizes first-party cookies (small text files stored on your device, such as <code class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">_ga</code> and <code class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">_ga_*</code>) to distinguish unique visitors and record aggregate traffic metrics across sessions.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            In addition, we use browser <code class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">localStorage</code> strictly for functional preferences: preserving your dark/light theme choice and your preferred measurement system (Metric vs. Imperial) so that your preferred unit settings persist between visits.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">4. Managing and Opting Out of Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            You have full control over cookie storage and analytics tracking:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            <li><strong>Browser Cookie Controls:</strong> You can configure your browser to block or delete cookies at any time via your browser settings.</li>
            <li><strong>Google Analytics Opt-Out:</strong> You can install the official <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-cyan-700 dark:text-cyan-400 underline hover:text-cyan-800 dark:hover:text-cyan-300">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a> to prevent data collection across all websites.</li>
            <li><strong>Content Blockers:</strong> Standard ad blockers and privacy extensions (such as uBlock Origin or browser tracking prevention) block analytics requests without impacting any calculator features.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">5. Hosting and Edge Infrastructure</h2>
          <p>
            Our static site assets are delivered globally via Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare processes transient HTTP connection metadata (IP addresses, request headers) strictly for essential security functions, including DDoS mitigation, bot defense, and edge caching.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">6. Clipboard Functionality</h2>
          <p>
            The &quot;Copy Workshop Recipe&quot; feature utilizes standard browser Clipboard APIs solely to copy the formatted text summary to your clipboard when you click the button. No clipboard contents are accessed, read, or transmitted.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">7. Contact Information</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions regarding this privacy policy or our analytics implementation, please contact us at <a href="mailto:support@epoxyresin-calculator.com" class="font-mono text-cyan-800 dark:text-cyan-400 underline">support@epoxyresin-calculator.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
